  "content": {
    "id": "p48-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Differentiate $y=(x^2-10)^3x^4$ using the chain rule and product rule.\n\nThen find points on the curve where the tangent is horizontal.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y'=10x^3(x^2-10)^2(x^2-4)$.\n\nThe points are $(0,0)$, $(\\sqrt{10},0)$, $(-\\sqrt{10},0)$, $(2,-3456)$ and $(-2,-3456)$.",
      "worked": "Let $u=(x^2-10)^3$ and $v=x^4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u'&=3(x^2-10)^2(2x)\\\\u'&=6x(x^2-10)^2\\\\v'&=4x^3.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the product rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\y'&=6x(x^2-10)^2x^4+4x^3(x^2-10)^3\\\\y'&=2x^3(x^2-10)^2[3x^2+2(x^2-10)]\\\\y'&=10x^3(x^2-10)^2(x^2-4).\\end{align*}$$\nA horizontal tangent has gradient zero:\n$$\\begin{align*}10x^3(x^2-10)^2(x^2-4)&=0\\\\x&=0,\\ \\pm\\sqrt{10},\\ \\pm2.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $y=(x^2-10)^3x^4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y(0)&=0\\\\y(\\pm\\sqrt{10})&=0\\\\y(\\pm2)&=(4-10)^3(\\pm2)^4\\\\y(\\pm2)&=-3456.\\end{align*}$$\nThe required points are $(0,0)$, $(\\sqrt{10},0)$, $(-\\sqrt{10},0)$, $(2,-3456)$ and $(-2,-3456)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
